        "Holding the rope close to the halter gives you direct control while keeping the remaining length folded (not wrapped) allows a quick release if the horse pulls or panics. Wrapping the rope around fingers or wrist risks serious injury if the horse moves suddenly. Clipping the rope to your belt or holding only the loose end reduces your ability to manage the horse safely.",
