        "Returning to basic flatwork helps the horse re-establish balance, contact and breathing in a controlled way. This reduces tension and restores rhythm so you can build back to more demanding work. Increasing intensity or using speed risks escalating stress or creating compensations, and cancelling or rushing to run without addressing balance may sacrifice welfare or performance.",
